ORIGIN

  https://rubygems.org/downloads/nokogiri-1.19.4.gem
  sha256 50c951611c92bca05c51411aef45f1cbc50f2821c4802758c5c6d34696533ab5

LOCAL CHANGES

  - ext/nokogiri/*.{c,h}  -> here (unmodified)
  - gumbo-parser/src/*    -> gumbo/ (unmodified)  nokogiri's bundled HTML5
                             parser; always linked, never optional
  - lib/**                -> lib/  (minus lib/nokogiri/jruby, JRuby only)
  - ports/ (the bundled libxml2/libxslt/zlib/libiconv tarballs) is NOT
    vendored. The extension links against third_party/libxml2 and
    third_party/libxslt, which are exactly the versions this gem pins in
    dependencies.yml (libxml2 2.13.9, libxslt 1.1.43).
  - extconf.rb is kept for reference only; it never runs (no mkmf, no
    dlopen). Its have_func() results are hand-transcribed into BUILD.mk.
  - nokogiri.gemspec is hand-written (upstream generates it with Rake).

  No .c or .h file has been modified.

RUNTIME DEPENDENCY WORTH KNOWING

  lib/nokogiri/css/parser.rb is a generated racc parser and does
  `require "racc/parser.rb"` at load time. racc ships with Ruby as a
  bundled gem whose gemspec is not installed in this build, so
  assemble_stdlib.sh copies racc/parser.rb and racc/info.rb into
  /zip/lib/ruby/4.0.0/racc/. racc's pure-Ruby engine is used (its
  cparse C extension is not compiled).
